[agent] No metric selection exists — Databricks Vector Search uses its native distance (L2-based) ranking, which is exactly the platform's native ANN. I'll use the Delta Sync self-managed approach. Let me set up: create a volume, upload the CSV, build the table via SQL.
[agent:bash] databricks volumes create --help 2>&1 | head -25
[agent:result] Create a Volume.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Creates a new volume.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   The user could create either an external volume or a managed volume. An
[agent:result]   external volume will be created in the specified external location, while a
[agent:result]   managed volume will be located in the default location which is specified by
[agent:result]   the parent schema, or the parent catalog, or the Metastore.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   For the volume creation to succeed, the user must satisfy following
[agent:result]   conditions: - The caller must be a metastore admin, or be the owner of the
[agent:result]   parent catalog and schema, or have the **USE_CATALOG** privilege on the parent
[agent:result]   catalog and the **USE_SCHEMA** privilege on the parent schema. - The caller
[agent:result]   must have **CREATE VOLUME** privilege on the parent schema.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   For an external volume, following conditions also need to satisfy - The caller
[agent:result]   must have **CREATE EXTERNAL VOLUME** privilege on the external location. -
[agent:result]   There are no other tables, nor volumes existing in the specified storage
[agent:result]   location. - The specified storage location is not under the location of other
[agent:result]   tables, nor volumes, or catalogs or schemas.
[agent:result] 
