[agent] ## Summary
[agent] I loaded the item embeddings into a Databricks Vector Search index and used its native ANN search to retrieve top-5 L2-nearest neighbors for every query.
[agent] **What I built (all in the per-run namespace `workspace.mlpab931b86`, prefix `mlpab931b86`):**
[agent] - **`workspace.mlpab931b86.itemsf3ae88_vol`** — managed volume holding the uploaded `items.csv`.
[agent] - **`workspace.mlpab931b86.itemsf3ae88_src`** — Delta table (CDF enabled), 300 rows, with the JSON-string embeddings parsed into `array<float>` (16-dim) via SQL.
[agent] - **`mlpab931b86_itemsf3ae88`** — Vector Search endpoint (STANDARD, prefixed).
[agent] - **`workspace.mlpab931b86.itemsf3ae88`** — the Delta-Sync self-managed vector index (the "store"), 300 rows indexed, `ready: true`.
[agent] **Process:**
[agent] - Loaded data platform-side through the `databricks` CLI (volume upload + SQL Statement Execution API to build the table).
[agent] - Created the endpoint and index; the first index build took ~17 min to provision (one stuck `HYBRID`-subtype attempt was deleted and recreated — note: `VECTOR` subtype is rejected, `HYBRID` is the only supported self-managed subtype).
[agent] - Queried the index's native similarity search (`/vector-search/indexes/.../query` with `query_vector`, `num_results=5`) for all 25 queries. Results come back ordered by score descending = L2 distance ascending (Databricks returns `1/(1+L2)`), so they are already nearest-first.
[agent] **Deliverable:** `submission/answers.json` — valid, with `store` set to the index name and all 25 query_ids each mapping to exactly 5 item_ids nearest-first (25 entries, 125 item references verified).
[agent] A couple of interface notes worth surfacing: the CLI's `vector-search-indexes query-index` command fails to unmarshal the query response (`invalid character 'r' after top-level value`), so I queried via `databricks api post` instead; and queries issued inside a `while … done < <(…)` loop failed TLS verification (CLI inheriting the process-substitution pipe as stdin) until I detached stdin with `< /dev/null`.
